# The fork child's orphaned cell: no thread of the child holds the cell
# a parent thread was discovering into (the forking-thread residue is in
# the axiom's doc).
axiom_cell_orphaned	platform/kernel fact	none (assumption)
# Runs until the reader reports the end or an error.
scan_lines	termination	none (assumption)
# The discovery scratch is the claim winner's alone: the record's PENDING->RUNNING
# exchange lets one thread through (the fork-child residue aside). The
# harness checks the reference is `DISCOVERY_SCRATCH`'s and writable.
discovery_scratch	allocator invariant	Kani	trusted (partly checked, Kani: sys::cgroup::kani_discovery_scratch::discovery_scratch_is_the_static; not checked: that no two references are live at once, which rests on the process having one `Deferred` record, whose exchange from `PENDING` to `RUNNING` lets one thread through to the item's one caller, `Deferred::cell_discover`, and which fails in the residue `axiom_cell_orphaned` states (a second discovery in the child of a `fork` from a signal handler that interrupted one, when the handler allocates))	contract 1688138844, body 141014262
# A raw in-place write, like `Arena::put_stats`: zero bytes are a valid
# `Cgroup`, then the state and the UNLIMITED stores. The harness runs the
# body on a slot of arbitrary bytes and checks its writes, the value's
# validity and the `ensures` (the test `untracked_in_place_is_untracked`
# compares the fields with `Cgroup::untracked`'s).
untracked_in_place	raw pointer (internal)	Kani	discharged (Kani: sys::cgroup::kani_in_place::untracked_in_place_is_untracked)	contract 2432176480, body 2334025224
